<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan Sugar buys U.S. corn, soybeans.</title>
<headline>Taiwan Sugar buys U.S. corn, soybeans.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-12-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-run Taiwan Sugar Corp bought 20,000 tonnes of U.S. corn and 10,000 tonnes of U.S. soybeans from Continental at a tender on Tuesday, traders said.  </p>
<p>The corn was bought at 117.24 U.S. cents over March Chicago futures and the soybeans at 126.94 U.S. cents over March Chicago futures, traders said.</p>
<p>The shipment was bought on a cost-and freight basis, traders said.</p>
<p>Shipment will be slated for January 15-31 from U.S. Gulf or February 1-15 from the Pacific Northwest.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
